Assessment of Treatment Plant Performance and Water Quality Data — von Sperling, Verbyla and Oliveira (@wu-performance: 0, is #reference, #part-of @wu-sources) { r_5PZG8VN422GHD657FBDR5KRWGS
Marcos von Sperling, Matthew E. Verbyla and Sílvia M. A. C. Oliveira. Assessment of Treatment Plant Performance and Water Quality Data: A Guide for Students, Researchers and Practitioners. IWA Publishing, January 2020. [Publisher and chapters](https://iwaponline.com/ebooks/book/777/Assessment-of-Treatment-Plant-Performance-and) · [DOI](https://doi.org/10.2166/9781780409320).

Read all fifteen chapters progressively. Begin with flow/loading, sampling and laboratory-data management; develop statistical interpretation and comparisons, then balances, loading rates, kinetics, reactor hydraulics and model assessment. Reproduce selected calculations independently and investigate cases where a removal percentage hides a changing influent load.

The publisher identifies CC BY-NC-ND 4.0 with component exceptions and supplies companion spreadsheets. Its indexed contents and edition were inspected; access to individual downloads can depend on the publisher host. Retain the actual version and distinguish a companion spreadsheet from independently checked evidence. The spreadsheets remain external.

